# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# BloodLink — Environment Variables Template
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# HOW TO USE
# ──────────
# 1. Copy this file to `.env` for local development:
#      cp .env.example .env
#
# 2. Fill in the values appropriate for your environment.
#
# 3. NEVER commit `.env`, `.env.local`, or any file containing real secrets.
#    Those files are already listed in .gitignore.
#    Only `.env.example` is safe to commit.
#
# VITE_* prefix rule
# ──────────────────
# Variables prefixed with VITE_ are bundled into the browser build and are
# therefore PUBLIC. Never put passwords, private keys, or secrets here.
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ─── Backend API URL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Controls the base URL that Axios uses for every API call.
#
# ┌──────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ Environment      │ Recommended value                                    │
# ├──────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
# │ Local dev        │ /api   (routes through Vite proxy — no CORS issues)  │
# │ Staging          │ https://api-staging.bloodlink.eg/api                 │
# │ Production       │ https://api.bloodlink.eg/api                         │
# └──────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
# When set to `/api` in development, Vite's dev-server proxy (configured in
# vite.config.ts › server.proxy) forwards requests to VITE_BACKEND_TARGET
# on the same machine, keeping the browser origin at localhost:5173 and
# eliminating all CORS pre-flight failures.
#
VITE_API_URL=/api

# ─── Mock Data Toggle ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Set to 'true' to use in-memory mock data (no backend required).
# Set to 'false' to connect to the real API endpoints.
#
VITE_USE_MOCK=true


# ─── Vite Dev Proxy Target ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The proxy target (backend host:port) is configured directly in
# vite.config.ts › server.proxy['/api'].target.
#
# Default value in vite.config.ts: http://localhost:3000
# Change it there if your backend runs on a different port:
#   NestJS    → 3000  (default)
#   Django    → 8000
#   Laravel   → 8000
#   Spring    → 8080
#
# This variable is kept here as a reminder; it is NOT read by Vite config
# because @types/node is not installed in this project (no process.env).
# Edit vite.config.ts directly instead.
#
# VITE_BACKEND_TARGET=http://localhost:3000
